1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Attacks move at machine speed. Network. Cloud. Agentic.
Identity. Response falls behind.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:11,500
AttackSentry changes the tempo.

3
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:20,000
It learns this network, then detects DDoS, brute force, C2,
and exfiltration in real time.

4
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:29,000
Every incident arrives with evidence, expert attribution, and
MITRE mapping. You see what changed, and why it matters.

5
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Respond with precision. Rate limit. Isolate. Block. With a
named target, an expiry, and an audit trail.

6
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:48,000
When behaviour is new, it is flagged as zero-day, not forced
into a known label. Our run: 21 known families, 3 zero-day
behaviours.

7
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:54,000
Mapped to NIST, ISO 27001, OWASP, and MITRE ATT&CK.

8
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:59,000
AttackSentry. Know what changed. Know what to do.
